<https://data.archives.gov.on.ca/KB/Agent/Ontario%20Telephone%20Services%20Commission> <https://www.ica.org/standards/RiC/ontology#history> "The Ontario Telephone Service Commission was formed on April 1, 1960 replacing the former Ontario Telephone Authority. It was located within the Department of Agriculture and Food. On 23 June 1971 it became part of the Department, later the Ministry, of Transportation and Communications. In 1987, it was moved to the Ministry of Culture and Communications, and finally became part of the Ministry of Economic Development and Trade in 1993 when that ministry became responsible for communications policy and programs. The Supreme Court of Canada ruled in Spring 1994 that communications was the responsibility of the CRTC (the federal communications regulatory body). The Ontario Telephone Services Commission was consequently closed down in the Fall of 1994." .
