<https://data.archives.gov.on.ca/KB/Agent/Northern%20Telephone%20Company> <https://www.ica.org/standards/RiC/ontology#history> "The Northern Telephone Company was founded in New Liskeard, Temiskaming District, Ontario on April 5, 1905. It was originally called the Temiskaming Telephone Company. Its range of customers expanded regularly over the next 50 years, through purchases of other telephone companies. The first of these was the Kirkland Lake and Swastika Telephone System, bought in 1921. In 1928 the company changed its name to Northern Telephone Company Limited. In 1966, Bell Canada acquired a controlling share in the company through stock purchases, although it continued to exist as a separate entity. In 1985 the company was still operational." .
